.TH SPEED-OF-CINNAMON 1 "June 2026" "speed-of-cinnamon 0.1.26" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
speed-of-cinnamon \- Cinnamon-native voice typing backend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B speed-of-cinnamon
.RI COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B speed-of-cinnamon
is the local Python backend used by the Speed of Cinnamon Cinnamon applet.
It records audio locally, runs a configurable speech recognition backend,
optionally post-processes the text, and reports state to the applet.
.PP
Normal desktop use is driven by the Cinnamon applet. The command line is useful
for setup checks, diagnostics, model management, backend-only tests, and
scripted maintenance.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Inspect runtime dependencies and the configured recorder, transcriber, output,
and post-processing pipeline.
.TP
.B setup
Build a copyable setup plan from a doctor report.
.TP
.B diagnostics
Collect a support bundle without transcript contents or private command
templates.
.TP
.B start
Start a recording and write state for the applet.
.TP
.B stop
Stop or finalize the current recording, transcribe it, and apply the selected
output mode.
.TP
.B toggle
Start recording when idle, or stop/finalize when recording.
.TP
.B cancel
Discard the current recording and remove local recording artifacts when they are
inside the Speed of Cinnamon recordings directory.
.TP
.B transcribe-file
Transcribe an existing local audio file without using the recorder.
.TP
.B list-inputs
List PipeWire/Pulse input source names through
.BR pactl (1).
.TP
.B models
List local CTranslate2 and GGML voice model catalog status.
.TP
.B download-model
Download and verify a catalog voice model.
.TP
.B remove-model
Remove a downloaded catalog model.
.TP
.B benchmark-models
Compare downloaded catalog voice models on one local audio file.
.TP
.B text-models
List local Ollama or OpenAI-compatible text models.
.TP
.B install-text-model
Install an Ollama text model.
.TP
.B history
List recent transcript files.
.TP
.B cleanup
Preview or remove old transcript files and cached recordings.
.TP
.B settings-export
Write a portable applet settings backup.
.TP
.B settings-import
Read a portable applet settings backup and restore local alarm state.
.TP
.B alarms
Manage Cinnamon-local repeating alarms. See
.BR speed-of-cinnamon-alarms (1).
.TP
.B insert-text
Send explicit text through the configured output path without recording or
transcribing audio.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed application version and exit.
.TP
.B --json
Print machine-readable JSON where supported.
.TP
.BI --state-file " PATH"
Use an alternate state file.
.TP
.BI --language " CODE"
Set the recognition language for the command.
.TP
.BI --insert-method " MODE"
Use
.BR clipboard-paste ,
.BR clipboard-only ,
.BR type ,
or
.BR none .
.TP
.BI --transcriber " BACKEND"
Use
.BR auto ,
.BR openai ,
.BR openai-whisper ,
.BR whisper ,
.BR whisper-cpp ,
.BR faster-whisper ,
.BR openai-compatible ,
.BR external-api ,
.BR command ,
.BR custom ,
or
.BR template .
The
.B whisper-cpp
backend accepts
.BR whisper-cli ,
.BR whisper.cpp ,
or Fedora
.BR pwcpp .
.PP
Compatibility aliases are normalized as:
.PP
.B openai
and
.B openai-whisper
map to
.B whisper ;
.B openai-compatible
and
.B external-api
map to
.B openai-compatible ;
.B faster-whisper
maps to
.B faster-whisper ;
.B custom
or
.B template
maps to
.B command .
.TP
.BI --transcriber-command " TEMPLATE"
Use a custom ASR command template.
.TP
.BR --openai-compatible-flex-processing ", " --no-openai-compatible-flex-processing
Enable or disable OpenAI Flex processing for
.B api.openai.com
speech-to-text and text-polishing requests. Enabled by default. The flag is not
sent to local OpenAI-compatible servers.
.SH CUSTOM COMMANDS
Custom transcriber and post-process templates are parsed into command argument
lists and are not executed through a shell. Limited
.B &&
chaining is supported. Shell operators and redirections such as
.BR | ,
.BR || ,
.BR & ,
.BR > ,
and
.B 2>
are rejected.
.PP
Transcriber templates can use:
.PP
.EX
{audio} {language} {text} {output_dir} {output_base}
.EE
.PP
Personalization placeholders are:
.PP
.EX
{context} {vocabulary} {prompt}
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run a setup-aware doctor check for applet mode:
.PP
.EX
speed-of-cinnamon doctor --applet --settings-json '{"transcriber":"command","transcriber-command":"printf ok","insert-method":"clipboard-paste"}' --json
.EE
.PP
Test transcription without inserting into the focused application:
.PP
.EX
speed-of-cinnamon toggle --insert-method none --transcriber command --transcriber-command "printf test"
.EE
.PP
Test only the output path:
.PP
.EX
speed-of-cinnamon insert-text "Hallo Terminal" --insert-method clipboard-paste --json
.EE
.PP
Preview cleanup:
.PP
.EX
speed-of-cinnamon cleanup --keep-transcripts 100 --keep-recordings 20 --dry-run --json
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/speed-of-cinnamon/state.json
Runtime state used by the applet.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/speed-of-cinnamon/transcripts/
Saved transcript history.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/speed-of-cinnamon/recordings/
Temporary recording files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/speed-of-cinnamon/models/whisper.cpp/
Downloaded whisper.cpp catalog models.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/speed-of-cinnamon/settings-export.json
Default portable settings backup.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/speed-of-cinnamon/alarms.json
Local repeating alarm store.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR speed-of-cinnamon-alarms (1),
.BR xdotool (1),
.BR pactl (1),
.BR pw-record (1)
